{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>Magdiel</b> — this is Rome; so is the language of Rashi. But I do not understand this, for if we say that it is a prophecy for many days and distant times, behold many kings ruled over Edom before the Roman empire, and Rome is not an <i>aluf</i> (chieftain), but rather it is a great kingdom, mighty, powerful, and exceedingly strong, unlike any among the kingdoms. But what they said in Pirkei Rabbi Eliezer (38): as a reward for having emptied his vessels for the sake of Jacob his brother, he was given a hundred provinces from Seir to Magdiel, and Magdiel is Rome, as it is said, \"the chief of Magdiel, the chief of Iram\" — their intent in this is what I have made known to you several times, that the events of the early ones were a sign for their descendants. And behold, these latter chiefs, ten together with Magdiel, alluded that the kings of Edom would be in their dominion during the fourth kingdom: ten would rule over the land of Edom, and the eleventh among them would rule over Rome, and from there their kingdom would subsequently spread over the entire world. And for this reason the name Magdiel alludes, that he shall magnify himself above every <i>El</i>, as it is said of him (Daniel 11:36), \"And the king shall do according to his will, and he shall exalt himself and magnify himself above every <i>El</i>.\" And this is what is said (Daniel 7:24), \"And the ten horns — from this kingdom ten kings shall arise, and another shall arise after them, and he shall be different from the former ones.\" And they said in Bereshit Rabbah (76:6): all of them the verse speaks of concerning those who came from the thigh of Esau, and they expounded (ibid. 83:4), \"the chief of Iram\" — that he is destined to pile up sieges against King Messiah, may he be revealed speedily:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:40:48.858657342Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}